# `codex/*` development sync

On `codex/*` branches, a local commit is not done until it is on origin.

After the primary thread creates a successful local commit of accepted work, immediately `git push` to the tracked origin branch (`git push origin HEAD` or the existing upstream). Do not wait for a per-session “please push”. GitHub `verify` CI and the connected Vercel Preview are part of this loop.

- Do not force-push.
- Do not push `main` or production.
- Subagents still must not commit, push, or deploy.
- Leave unrelated dirty files unstaged; do not stash them into the pushed commit.
- `pnpm development:infra` is a separate step. It needs a clean, already-pushed HEAD. Run it when reconciling the isolated stack or protected synthetic acceptance, not instead of `git push`.
